ecked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[42,1788][103,1825]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="1" text="09-11 23:07" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="dev.leonardo.ocbeacon.dev" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[124,1790][290,1824]" drawing-order="1" hint="" /><node index="2" text='Today&apos;s date is now: Fri Sep 11 2026&#10;&#10;The Code Mode tool catalog has changed. This catalog supersedes the previous Code Mode tool catalog.&#10;&#10;The Code Mode tool catalog below is partial.&#10;&#10;The Code Mode catalog and `search` results are the complete set of tools callable inside `execute`. It does not affect tools exposed directly outside Code Mode.&#10;&#10;## Search&#10;&#10;Use `search` to discover exact paths and signatures for additional tools:&#10;&#10;- search(input: {&#10;  query?: string,&#10;  namespace?: string,&#10;  /** @integer @exclusiveMinimum 0 */&#10;  limit?: number,&#10;  /** @integer @minimum 0 */&#10;  offset?: number,&#10;}): {&#10;  items: Array&lt;{&#10;      path: string,&#10;      description: string,&#10;      signature: string,&#10;    }&gt;,&#10;  /** @integer @minimum 0 */&#10;  remaining: number,&#10;  next: {&#10;      /** @integer @minimum 0 */&#10;      offset: number,&#10;    } | null,&#10;}&#10;&#10;## Available tools&#10;&#10;- agentmemory (7 tools, 2 shown)&#10;  - tools.agentmemory.memory_export(input: {}): Promise&lt;unknown&gt; // Export all memory data as JSON.&#10;  - tools.agentmemory.memory_sessions(input: {}): Promise&lt;unknown&gt; // List recent sessions with their status and observation counts.&#10;- context7 (2 tools, 1 shown)&#10;  - tools.context7["resolve-library-id"](input: {&#10;  /**&#10;   * What to look up in the library&apos;s documentation. This is used to rank library results by relevance to what the user is trying to accomplish. The query is sent to the Context7 API for processing. Do not include any sensitive or confidential information such as API keys, passwords, credentials, personal data, or proprietary code in your query.&#10;   */&#10;  query: string,&#10;  /**&#10;   * Library name to search for and retrieve a Context7-compatible library ID. Use the official library name with proper punctuation — e.g., &apos;Next.js&apos; instead of &apos;nextjs&apos;, &apos;Customer.io&apos; instead of &apos;customerio&apos;, &apos;Three.js&apos; instead of &apos;threejs&apos;.&#10;   */&#10;  libraryName: string,&#10;}): Promise&lt;unknown&gt; // Resolves a package/product name to a Context7-compatible library ID and returns matching libraries.&#10;- dbhub (2 tools, 1 shown)&#10;  - tools.dbhub.execute_sql(input: {&#10;  /** SQL to execute (multiple statements separated by ;) */&#10;  sql: string,&#10;}): Promise&lt;unknown&gt; // 本地 SQLite 调试库（自动创建）. Execute SQL queries on the sqlite database&#10;- duckduckgo (3 tools, 2 shown)&#10;  - tools.duckduckgo.expand_link(input: {&#10;  token: string,&#10;}): Promise&lt;{&#10;  result: string,&#10;}&gt; // Expand a shortened ref://&lt;id&gt; link token from search results back into the full URL. Search results replace very long...&#10;  - tools.duckduckgo.search(input: {&#10;  query: string,&#10;  /** @default 10 @integer */&#10;  max_results?: number,&#10;  /** @default "" */&#10;  region?: string,&#10;}): Promise&lt;{&#10;  result: string,&#10;}&gt; // Search the web using DuckDuckGo. Returns a list of results with titles, URLs, and snippets. Use this to find current ...&#10;- grep (1 tool)&#10;  - tools.grep.searchGitHub(input: {&#10;  /**&#10;   * The literal code pattern to search for (e.g., &apos;useState(&apos;, &apos;export function&apos;). Use actual code that would appear in files, not keywords or ques